Design a circuit that converts an 8-bit binary number to its corresponding Gray code representation. The conversion is performed synchronously on the rising edge of the clock, where the most significant bit of the Gray code is directly taken from the binary input, and each subsequent bit is generated by XORing adjacent bits of the binary number.
