description:
Design a pipeline register system that operates with a specified data width (default is 8 bits) and a configurable depth (default is 4 stages). On every rising edge of the clock signal, the data input is shifted through multiple stages of registers, with the newest data being inserted at the first stage and all other data shifting one stage deeper in the pipeline. The output provides the data stored in the last stage of the pipeline, effectively allowing for latency management and the implementation of a simple delay mechanism for digital signals in sequential circuits.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [width-1:0] data_in,
  output [width-1:0] data_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input [width-1:0] data_in,
  output [width-1:0] data_out
);parameter width = 8; // width of the data signal
parameter depth = 4; // depth of the pipeline register

reg [width-1:0] pipeline [0:depth-1];

integer i;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  for (i = depth-1; i > 0; i = i - 1) begin
    pipeline[i] <= pipeline[i-1];
  end
  pipeline[0] <= data_in;
end

assign data_out = pipeline[depth-1];

endmodule

