description:
Design a clock divider that takes an input clock signal and produces a lower frequency output clock by a specified division ratio. The module features a reset input to initialize the divider and the output clock. On each rising edge of the input clock, the internal counter increments, and once it reaches the value of the divide ratio minus one, it resets the counter and toggles the output clock signal, effectively creating a square wave output at a frequency that is the input frequency divided by the defined ratio.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter divide_ratio = 2;

reg [31:0] count;

always @(posedge clk_in or posedge reset) begin
  if (reset) begin
    count <= 0;
    clk_out <= 0;
  end else begin
    count <= count + 1;
    if (count == divide_ratio - 1) begin
      count <= 0;
      clk_out <= ~clk_out;
    end
  end
end

endmodule

