description:
Design a frequency divider that takes an input clock signal and produces an output clock signal at a frequency reduced by a factor of 'n'. The module uses a counter to track the number of input clock cycles, toggling the output clock signal once the count reaches 'n-1', effectively halving the frequency if 'n' is set to 2. The output clock toggles on every 'n' input clock cycles, enabling the creation of lower frequency timing signals for various applications in digital circuits.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter n = 2; // division factor

  reg [31:0] count;

  always @(posedge clk_in) begin
    if (count == n-1) begin
      clk_out <= ~clk_out;
      count <= 0;
    end else begin
      count <= count + 1;
    end
  end

endmodule

