Design a 3-to-8 binary decoder that activates one of eight outputs based on a 3-bit input, abc, synchronized with the rising edge of a clock signal. For each unique value of abc from 000 to 111, the corresponding output line in the 8-bit output y is set high (logic 1), while all other outputs remain low (logic 0). This decoder effectively translates a 3-bit input code into a single active output line, enabling applications such as memory address decoding or control signal generation in digital circuits.
