description:
Design a digital circuit that implements a Johnson counter (also known as a twisted ring counter) with a parameterized number of bits, specified by the parameter `n`. The counter shifts its state on each clock cycle, generating a unique sequence of output states by using XOR feedback from certain bits of the shift register. Specifically, it takes the inverse of the last two bits and combines them with the other bits to determine the next state, ensuring that only valid sequences are produced. The output reflects the current state of the shift register, allowing for the observation of the Johnson counting sequence.
module top_module(
  input clock,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clock,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] shift_reg;
wire [n-1:0] next_state;

assign next_state[0] = shift_reg[n-1] ^ shift_reg[n-2];
assign next_state[n-1] = shift_reg[n-2] ^ shift_reg[n-3];

genvar i;
generate
  for (i = 1; i < n-1; i = i+1) begin
    assign next_state[i] = shift_reg[i-1] ^ shift_reg[i] ^ shift_reg[i+1];
  end
endgenerate

always @(posedge clock) begin
  shift_reg <= next_state;
end

assign out = shift_reg;

endmodule

