Design a circuit that serves as a 2-bit binary counter with enable functionality. The counter increments its value on the falling edge of a slower clock (clk_lento) when enabled (hab_in). If the counter reaches the maximum value of 3 (2'b11), it wraps around to 0. The counter's current value is output on index_out, and transitions are controlled by the fast clock (clk_50) to sample the slower clock's state.
